SUMMARY:🧪 Lab | Mastering GitHub Copilot Across the Software Development
  Life Cycle (SDLC)
LOCATION:Online
DESCRIPTION:Practice using GitHub Copilot throughout the software developme
 nt life cycle in this advanced (L300) hands-on lab. Guided exercises cover
  feature planning\, codebase exploration\, unit tests\, goal-oriented deve
 lopment with Agent mode\, delegated coding tasks\, code review\, security 
 remediation\, MCP servers\, and custom instructions and prompt files. The 
 public registration page includes a pre-event machine-access test.\n\nTopi
 cs:\n- Plan features and explore a codebase with GitHub Copilot\n- Write u
 nit tests and use Chat in Ask\, Edit\, and Agent modes\n- Delegate develop
 ment tasks to the Copilot coding agent\n- Review code and remediate vulner
 abilities with Copilot Autofix\n- Extend context with MCP servers\, custom
  instructions\, and prompt files\n\nAudience: Developers seeking advanced 
 (L300)\, hands-on experience with GitHub Copilot across the software devel
 opment life cycle.\n\nRegistration is required and subject to approval.\n\
 nThis series calendar is for discovery\, not registration. Entries are mar
 ked Free. Register separately for the sessions you want to attend.\n\nRegi
 ster: https://msevents.microsoft.com/event?id=1908106858
